{title: Down in the Belly of the Fish}
{subtitle: Jonah 2:1–11; 1:1–16; 3:1–5}
{key: C}
{tempo: 119}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [–] | [C] | [F] |
| [C] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]God said, Jonah, go [F]to Nine[C]veh
Jonah ran the other [G]way
[C]Hopped aboard a ship [F]to Tarshish
[G]Sailing far, far a[C]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Whoosh went the wind and splash [F]went the [C]waves
The ship began to creak and [G]shake
The [C]sailors cried, but [F]Jonah slept
[G]Down below, not yet a[C]wake
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Over the side went Jon[G]ah, splash
And the [C]stormy sea [G/B]grew [Am]calm
Then a[F]long came a great big [C]fish
And gulp, it [D]swallowed Jonah [G]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Down, down in the bel[F]ly of the [C]fish
Three days and three [G]nights
[C]Jonah called to God [F]from way down [C]deep
And God heard [G]him, [C]God heard [G]him
[F]Clap your [G]hands, God [C]heard him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In [F]my distress I called [G]to the LORD, [C]and he [G/B]answered [Am]me
Sal[F]vation belongs to [G]the LORD
[C]Splash, the fish spat [G]Jonah out
Onto [C]dry land
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Then God spoke to Jonah a [F]second [C]time
Get up, go to Nine[G]veh
[C]This time Jonah [F]got right [C]up
And [G]off he went to Nine[C]veh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Down, down in the bel[F]ly of the [C]fish
Three days and three [G]nights
[C]Jonah called [F]to God from [C]way down deep
And God [G]heard [C]him, God heard [G]him
[F]Clap your [G]hands, God [C]heard him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
A second time, a [F]second [C]chance
God heard [G]him, God [C]heard him
{end_of_verse}
